Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.309 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  once i've found an interesting lesson i  open it in the link reader  i can see how many new words there are  for me in lesson  these words are blue  as i read i click on blue words i don't  know  this shows me popular translations for  these words  these are the translations that have  been used most often by link members  this one looks good  now on to the next blue word  if i'm not happy with the popular  translations shown i can click the  available dictionaries and create my own  notice that when i add a translation the  blue words turn yellow  yellow words are called links and they  stay yellow until i've learned them  i continue until i have removed all the  blue either by creating links or making  words known  at any time if i know all remaining blue  words on a page  turning a page moves them all to known  automatically  if i accidentally move a word to known  no big deal  i just click on it to make a link with  it  when moving to the next page the  integrated vocabulary review pops up  this lets me review all yellow links  from the page before moving on  this quick step lets me quickly review  these links while they are still fresh  i continue my lesson creating links and  making words known until all blue words  are gone  when all blue words are gone i complete  the lesson  i can give the lesson a rose to  recommend it to other link members in  their feeds  now i go back and listen to the lesson  while reading along  clicking in the progress bar takes me  back to the first page quickly  at a certain point i'm ready to move on  to my next lesson  i don't need to understand the lesson  perfectly i know that it will all become  clearer over time with enough exposure  and linking  the more reading and listening i do the  fewer blue words i see and the closer i  get to fluency  happy linking

